  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRA Somalia Protracted Crisis Joint Response 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HealthThe project seeks to improve access to lifesaving primary healthcare services for internally displaced persons (IDPs) and vulnerable host communities. NutritionThe goal is to address acute malnutrition among children under five and pregnant and lactating women (PLW).WASHImproving access to clean water, sanitation, and hygiene practices is essential. Food Security and LivelihoodsEnhancing food security and agricultural productivity. ProtectionStrengthening community and stakeholder capacity to prevent and respond to protection risks.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a comprehensive, multi-sectoral intervention designed to address the critical needs of vulnerable populations in Somalia. Through targeted health, nutrition, WASH, FSL, and protection activities, the project aims to improve the well-being and resilience of crisis-affected communities, while ensuring sustainable and locally-led development.</narrative>
  </description>
